provenance note. This job's params (savedSearchId, reportRuleId, execution range, spec
  sha256) are identical to job 01M1C5YHT1G491DDGG8DJVEKQZ of 2026-08-31, and the dataset
  differs only in its fetch stamps: all 652 rows compare byte-identical, with only
  fetchedAt (2026-08-31T15:10:34.281Z -> 2026-09-02T13:41:19.329Z) and execution.resolvedAt
  changed. The idempotencyKey differs, so this is a distinct job and was run, not skipped.
  The pipeline was rebuilt independently here rather than copied; every deterministic
  figure below reproduces that run exactly (counts, lexicon, keyword pass, clustering,
  concentration, suffixes, redirects, ranking, linkage). The one axis that differs is the
  §4.4 reasoning pass, which is a judgement, not a computation — see below.

ingest (§1). The gateway feed is JSON, not the semicolon CSV the spec describes, so its
fields were mapped onto the required columns:
  Domain <- name | URL <- currentDecision.url | Source <- currentDecision.initialAuthor
  Rank <- details.trancoListRanking | Updated at <- updatedAt
  Confidence <- details.confidencePercent | LLM Reasoning <- details.reasons joined
  Case Management Status <- caseManagement.currentState
  Status <- details.classification, normalised per the §1 table:
    ALLOWS_ONLINE_GAMBLING 118 -> Gambling
    NO_ALLOWS_ONLINE_GAMBLING 336 -> Not gambling
    UNAVAILABLE 168 -> Unreachable
    REQUIRE_MORE_ANALYSIS 4 -> Review needed
    null (workflow ANALYSIS_ERROR) 26 -> Unknown
  Status is taken from the classification rather than the workflow state (BLACKLISTED 116 /
  WHITELISTED 297 / REVIEW_NEEDED 213 / ANALYSIS_ERROR 26) because the spec's Status values
  are gambling-classification values; the classification mapping also populates every branch
  of the table, whereas the workflow state leaves Unreachable empty and would discard the
  168 rows the crawler could not reach.
  optional columns: Interesting Keywords <- details.tags; Remarks <- currentStep.comment
  (empty throughout). Legal entity and legal-entity country are absent from the feed, so
  they are never inferred: blocklist rows carry null.
  §0 normalisation: caseManagement ILLEGAL_GAMBLING (116 rows) normalised to "Gambling" on
  ingest. Rows arriving as Licensed gambling: 0 (license is null on all 652 rows). No
  legal/illegal/licensed axis, label, header or metric name appears anywhere in the report.
  encoding: UTF-8 verified, 66 rows carry Thai script intact, 0 mojibake.
  required columns present: 9/9.

working set (§3): 652 raw - 4 Review needed = 648; 0 duplicate URLs dropped. total=648.

lexicon (§2, Appendix A): parsed directly out of the spec's Appendix A tables rather than
  transcribed, to remove any risk of copy error. 14 categories, 291 entries,
  286 distinct — matches the spec's own stated count of 286.
  5 cross-tab duplicates (คาสิโน, คาสิโนออนไลน์, พนันกีฬา, พนันบอล, แทงบอล) resolved to the
  specific product tab per §2.4; รูเล็ตออนไลน์ counted once (Casino = 14 distinct).
  Loaded as found: nothing added, translated or extended. suggestedLexiconAdditions: none.
  matching (§2.3/A.3): Thai = case-sensitive substring; Latin = case-insensitive on a
  token boundary; mixed (สล็อต pg, จับยี่กี VIP) = substring, case-insensitively, since a
  boundary test is meaningless around Thai; hashtags matched with '#' then re-run stripped
  against the product tabs (§4.3).
  short abbreviations PG PP FC XO SA WM AG AE: confined to the Domain/URL text and matched
  only as a whole domain segment or at a segment edge. The spec's own example `slotxo` shows
  a stem edge counts with no separator present, which is what reconciles "stands alone or at
  a separator inside a domain stem" with "a bare occurrence inside running prose does not
  count". A prose-boundary reading would have missed FC on qpfc.com.
  Abbreviations matches: BET 28, WALLET 10, RTP 8, WIN 7, VIP 4, FC 1 (58 total).
  §2.3 flag: BET accounts for 48.3% of Abbreviations matches — over the
  20% mark, so flagged as a probable false-positive source (it matches the standalone word
  "bet" in classifier prose).

subcategory and signal tags (§4):
  530 non-gambling rows -> "Not applicable", method n/a, no tags (§4.1).
  118 gambling rows: 45 assigned by keyword (§4.2), 73 by the reasoning pass (§4.4).
  0 rows hit §4.4 constraint 6 ("Unspecified"): every gambling row has reasoning text.
  reasoning pass: reasons arrive as clauses prefixed "Screenshot:" and "URL:";
  URL-attributed clauses are excluded from the product judgement per constraint 2, which is
  branding rather than offering. Product terms are read out of the reasoning itself and are
  never added to the lexicon. Primary offering = most mentions, then earliest mention, then
  A.1 order; the rest go to subcategoryAlternatives (constraint 3). Constraint 5 applied
  where the reasoning describes a site listing/reviewing/linking other gambling sites.
  Each inferred row carries a subcategoryBasis quoting the phrase that drove it (constraint 8).
  distribution: Football Betting 40 (21 kw / 19 inferred) | Casino 35 (4 kw / 31 inferred) | Slots 28 (17 kw / 11 inferred) | General Gambling 9 (2 kw / 7 inferred) | Lottery 2 (0 kw / 2 inferred) | Playing card 2 (0 kw / 2 inferred) | Baccarat 2 (1 kw / 1 inferred)
